---
scope: "The QUIESCENCE of a widget-hosted child Claude instance, decomposed into the two halves the predecessor fused: MEASUREMENT, which needs the child's byte stream and is therefore local to whoever hosts it, and NUDGING, which is a semantic act needing nothing but the bus. Covers the heartbeat as BUILT, the four residual gaps measured on 2026-08-13 (no cadence readback, an accidental cadence identity axis, an unproven nudge delivery, and idle's total invisibility), the invariant that a nudge is never activity, and the six design-decision nodes — four OPEN, one ratified by David on 2026-08-13, one settled earlier — that the architect ratifies before any build."
audience: "the builder wiring the hosted child's cadence readback, its quiescence publication and its channel nudge; the composeux-architect ratifying the four open DD forks; anyone who reads that a hosted child 'has no quiescence tracking' and needs the measured correction"
boundary: "IN: the measure/nudge decomposition and why it is the load-bearing content; the nudge as a CHANNEL message rather than a PTY keystroke, and the announce-then-bind design check that argues for it; the invariant that a nudge must not reset the idle clock, restated across a transport boundary; which identity axis the cadence config keys on; the readback that makes a configured cadence distinguishable from a defaulted one; idle observability on bus and glass; the display-state naming collision; the boundary matrix and the acceptance bar. OUT: `HarnessMonitor`'s own tier logic and echo-grace semantics ([CXC-IC-HEARTBEAT-CADENCE] — consumed unchanged, never forked); the context-threshold half of the same monitor ([CXC-TERM-CHILD-TELEMETRY]); the single-write-site and injection-log contracts ([CXC-TERM-CONVERGE] — untouched, because nothing here writes to a PTY); away-watch idle tracking ([SPEC:CXC-IDLE-TRACKING] — a different clock over a different subject)."
not-this: "Not a claim that the hosted child has no quiescence tracking — that was the starting hypothesis and MEASUREMENT REFUTED IT ([CXC-CQ-AS-BUILT]). Not a keystroke-injection design: a nudge into a hosted child is a bus message on the child's channel, and [CXC-CQ-NUDGE-TRANSPORT] states the four reasons plus the platform-spine argument that settles it. Not a second monitor: every requirement here is a wiring argument to the ONE shared `ptycore.build_monitor`, and a widget-local heartbeat implementation is a review reject for the reason [CXC-TERM-CHILD-TELEMETRY] already gave. Not a redefinition of idle: idle remains CONTINUOUS idle since the last GENUINE child output. Not away-watch idle: [SPEC:CXC-IDLE-TRACKING] measures the HUMAN's dead clock to size a work queue; this measures a CHILD INSTANCE's dead clock to decide whether to nudge it."
